// The gallery's board game room on level 2 (layout.puck's galleryGameStations: twelve stations in two rows of six), all
// twelve (`galleryRoomStationsIn`): each the debug world set's station (../game-stations.puck) holding its own games,
// chess, whose pieces its holodeck stands on the glass as bodies while chess is shown, and Klondike and FreeCell, whose
// cards it stands the same way. Every station plays one set of rules, each station's game its own, so a move at one
// station never touches another. The debug world stands only the first (../game-station-deck.puck), so its floors leave
// this module out. ../game-station.md says how to play and drive them.
//
// A module library: `galleryGames(frame)` stands the twelve where the frame stands the building, each turned with it,
// and building.puck expands it on a floor that enables `gameStations`. A station stands at its own size, since the
// standard's station takes no scale. The document that expands the building declares the chess game's vocabularies
// itself (`PieceKind`, `MoveKind`, `TurnColor`, as ../game-stations.puck's header gives them): a template's rules fold an
// enum's members only when the expanding source declares the enum (gallery-root.puck), and holds room in its
// `bodies.capacity` for each station's largest game (`gameStationBodies` a station).

import "layout"
import "../game-stations"

template galleryGames(frame) {
  let stations = galleryRoomStationsIn(frame)

  gameStationSet(stations: stations)

  // At the first station's near chair (a1), 1.5 m from its centre at its -Z edge and facing +Z across the glass, inside
  // the engage radius: the context button sits her down.
  spawnPoints [
    {
      id: "cards"
      position: gameStationChairAt(stations[0], "near")
      yawDegrees: gameStationChairYaw(stations[0], "near")
    }
    {
      id: "chess"
      position: gameStationChairAt(stations[0], "near")
      yawDegrees: gameStationChairYaw(stations[0], "near")
    }
  ]
}
